  "title": "Divisibility of central binomial coefficients",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem (1) Prove that there exist infinitely many positive integers $n$ such that $$\\gcd({2n\\choose n}, 3\\cdot 5\\cdot 7) = 1.$$\n\nProblem (2) Prove that there exists only a finite number of positive integers $n$ such that $$\\gcd({2n\\choose n}, 3\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot 11) = 1.$$",
